# =============================================================================
# North Forge - Hermes Edition (Kyocera Edition v21.8) - part of the North
# Forge project.
# File: .gitignore | Version: 1.0.1 | Updated: 2026-09-05
# Author: Kenneth C. Walker Jr. - Senior Technical Support Engineer, TSC
# =============================================================================

# Secrets - never commit
.env
*.env
.hermes.override.md
AGENTS.override.md

# Per-drive mode toggle - local to each physical drive, never synced via git
# (a git pull overwriting a Sales drive's toggle back to a committed value
# would be exactly the failure this whole system exists to prevent)
.forge-mode
.agent-name
.provider-choice
.readme-shown
.drive-record.txt
# Drive-root launcher shortcut - generated per drive by launch-north-forge.bat
# and provision-new-drive.ps1; its target path is drive-letter-specific, so it
# must never be committed (same reason as the per-drive markers above).
/North Forge.lnk

# Generated at each launch from skills-source/ + .hermes.template.md + mode-blocks/
# - these are build artifacts, not source. Never edit them directly; edit the
# source and re-launch. .hermes/ here is a PROJECT-LOCAL folder (the exact
# name Hermes scans for project skills) - unrelated to the user's global
# ~/.hermes profile directory.
/.hermes/
/.hermes-home/
.hermes.md

# Hermes runtime/state - this repo holds the content layer only,
/.hermes-home/
# not per-machine state, memory, sessions, or logs
# Complete per-drive engine installation and runtime state (root-anchored).
/.hermes-home/
# Bare (unanchored) rule so any RUNTIME config.yaml nested somewhere under
# this checkout (e.g. a stray .hermes-home/ copy) stays ignored. The
# repo-ROOT config.yaml is different: since the 2026-09-11 restructuring to
# a plain Hermes profile distribution, this repo is never itself a live
# HERMES_HOME (that's <HERMES_HOME>/profiles/kyocera/, outside the repo
# entirely) - so root config.yaml is distribution-seed content (defaults
# copied into a profile only on a FRESH `hermes profile install`, see
# profile_distribution.py), not runtime state. Un-ignore just that one path.
config.yaml
!/config.yaml
state.db
state.db-*
sessions/
memories/
cron/
# Anchored to .hermes-home/ (Hermes engine log dir). A bare "logs/" here
# also silently ignored the tracked repo-root logs/ folder that holds the
# session audit reports (folder renamed from audit/ -> logs/ on 2026-09-05).
# "*.log" below still catches stray Hermes log files written anywhere else.
/.hermes-home/logs/
*.log

# OS/editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/

# Claude Code's own settings dir - keeping this in the repo's own .gitignore
# makes the repo self-contained instead of depending on a machine-global
# git config to exclude it
.claude/

# REMOVED 2026-09-13 (Zone A fix): the /skills/ guard here was written when
# skills-source/ was the real tracked source dir and a stray root-level
# skills/ was a wrong-named build artifact. d4b0abc (2026-09-11) flattened
# skills-source/ INTO skills/ - skills/ is now the real, intentional tracked
# source dir. The old guard had started silently shadowing it: existing
# tracked files stayed tracked (gitignore does not retroactively untrack),
# but any NEW file added under skills/ since 2026-09-11 would be silently
# dropped by a plain git add, no error. Found while fixing the fault-logging
# branding leak this session (git add warned the path was ignored).
# git status --ignored confirmed nothing was actually lost under skills/.

# Drive-local Hermes installer runtime state written by scripts/ensure-hermes.ps1
# / scripts/ensure-hermes.sh. Per-drive, generated at install time, never source.
# "*.log" above already catches files inside install-logs/, but not the
# directory itself nor the staged installer script it also writes
# (hermes-installer-*.ps1) - so all three are named explicitly here.
/.hermes-install-incomplete
/.hermes-install-staging/
/install-logs/

# kb-builder's draft output (skills/kb-builder, Zone B - the write location itself
# isn't scripted, so it can't be redirected here). Ignoring the folder is the Zone A
# fix available: real technician use was writing drafts into this tracked working
# tree, polluting `git status` on every session. Untracked-but-ignored here either
# way - a draft is working output, never source to commit.
/kb-drafts/
